<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Aligned inverse sampling</h3>

<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inverse Sampling.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},\ldots,c_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},\ldots,c_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the identified clusters, and let <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(c_{1}),\ldots,\Pr(c_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(c_{1}),\ldots,\Pr(c_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the sum of the token probabilities within them, such that <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(c_{i})=\sum_{x\in c_{i}}P_{M}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(c_{i})=\sum_{x\in c_{i}}P_{M}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. It is natural to map these probabilities onto the interval [0,1] and employ inverse sampling to pseudo-randomly select a number <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> seeded by the watermark code <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. The subsequent token is then sampled from cluster <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> falls within the interval <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}\Pr(c_{j}),\sum_{j=0}^{i}\Pr(c_{j})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}\Pr(c_{j}),\sum_{j=0}^{i}\Pr(c_{j})]</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(c_{0}):=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(c_{0}):=0</annotation></semantics></math>. During detection, cluster information and the pseudo-random number <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> can be reconstructed using the watermark code <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing us to compute a statistical score by comparing the cluster against <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, since token probabilities are unknown during watermark detection, we cannot ascertain the cluster probabilities <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(c_{1}),\ldots,\Pr(c_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(c_{1}),\ldots,\Pr(c_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. This discrepancy leads to an alignment issue between <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and the identified cluster <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, as it becomes uncertain whether <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is within the interval <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}\Pr(c_{j}),\sum_{j=0}^{i}\Pr(c_{j})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\sum_{j=0}^{i-1}\Pr(c_{j}),\sum_{j=0}^{i}\Pr(c_{j})]</annotation></semantics></math>. To address this, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christ et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kuditipudi et al. (2023)</a></cite> proposed a position-based statistical score for watermark detection. The underlying principle is that if <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is close to 1, then the index of the selected cluster during watermark generation is likely close to <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> (the end of the clusters). However, the detection methods proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kuditipudi et al. (2023)</a></cite> cannot provide a theoretical guarantee of the false positive rate.
Besides, this position-based score has shown low detectability, as evidenced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kuditipudi et al. (2023)</a></cite> and our experimental findings. To address the flaws of inverse sampling, we introduce aligned inverse sampling, which substantially improves detection efficiency while providing a provable guarantee on the false-positive rate.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Aligned Inverse Sampling.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the scenario where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(c_{1})=\cdots=\Pr(c_{h})=\frac{1}{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(c_{1})=\cdots=\Pr(c_{h})=\frac{1}{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this case, the pseudo-random number <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and the identified cluster <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are aligned. Specifically, if <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)\in\left[\frac{i-1}{h},\frac{i}{h}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)\in\left[\frac{i-1}{h},\frac{i}{h}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, the detector can confidently assert that <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> was generated through inverse sampling with <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. A natural enhancement to inverse sampling involves rearranging the cluster probabilities within the interval [0,1] to emulate this aligned scenario.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Details on this method are in Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ Appendix B Missing Algorithms ‣ Robust Distortion-Free Watermark for Autoregressive Audio Generation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Aligned inverse sampling is a distortion-free watermark.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is straightforward. As aligned inverse sampling does not modify the cluster probability, by the property of inverse sampling, we have <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{M}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[P_{W}(x|\theta)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{M}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[P_{W}(x|\theta)]</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">With the aforementioned probability assignments, we can define a statistical score for the detector based on the pseudo-random number <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and the current token <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the pseudo-random number <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and the current token <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the detection score <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(r,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(r,x)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(r,x):=\left\{\begin{array}[]{cl}1&amp;\text{if }r\in\left[\frac{i-1}{h},\frac{i}{h}\right],\text{ where }x\in c_{i},\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mtext> where </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(r,x):=\left\{\begin{array}[]{cl}1&amp;\text{if }r\in\left[\frac{i-1}{h},\frac{i}{h}\right],\text{ where }x\in c_{i},\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Note, when <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(c_{i})&lt;\frac{1}{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(c_{i})&lt;\frac{1}{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, aligned inverse sampling may sample tokens from clusters other than <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> even if the pseudo-random number <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> falls within <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\frac{i-1}{h},\frac{i}{h}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\frac{i-1}{h},\frac{i}{h}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. This can reduce detection accuracy. However, empirical results indicate that the overall detectability of aligned inverse sampling still surpasses that of the regular inverse sampling reweight strategy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Aligned-IS</span> generator.</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> secret key <span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">key</span>, prompt <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{-m:0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{-m:0}</annotation></semantics></math>, generate length <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, token-audio decoder <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              Initialize watermark code history <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="hist" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">hist</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,t</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
                Calculate the token distribution for generating the <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{M}(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{-m:i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{M}(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{-m:i-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
                Generate a watermark code <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}=(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}=(</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">key<math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext=",\bm{x}_{i-n,i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">,\bm{x}_{i-n,i-1})</annotation></semantics></math></span>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}\in hist" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}\in hist</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
                 Sample the next token <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> using original distribution <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{M}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{-m:i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{M}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{-m:i-1})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
                
                
                 Generate the pseudo-random number <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
                
                
                 Calculate watermarked distribution <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{W}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{-m:i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{-m:i-1})</annotation></semantics></math> via aligned inverse sampling.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
                
                
                 Sample the next token <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> using distribution <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{W}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{-m:i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{W}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{-m:i-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
  
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> audio waveform <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D(\bm{x}_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(\bm{x}_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> <span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Aligned-IS</span> detector.</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> audio waveform <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, audio-token encoder <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, secret key <span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">key</span>, score function <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, threshold <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              calculate token sequence <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{1:t}=E(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1:t}=E(a)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              Initialize the score function: <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=0</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=2,...,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=2,...,t</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
                Generate the watermark code <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}=(\textrm{key},\bm{x}_{i-n,i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>key</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}=(\textrm{key},\bm{x}_{i-n,i-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
                Generate the pseudo-random number <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
                Update the score function via <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=S+s(r(\theta_{i}),x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=S+s(r(\theta_{i}),x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S&gt;z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S&gt;z</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span><span id="S4.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Aligned-IS</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the aligned inverse sampling reweight strategy, we can construct our watermarking algorithm <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Aligned-IS</span>. <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Aligned-IS</span> consists of a watermark generator and a watermark detector. In the watermark generator, the watermarked token at step <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is generated using a secret key <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">key</span> and the prior n-gram content <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t-n,t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t-n,t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> as the watermark code <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The pseudo-random number <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is then generated based on <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Following the inverse sampling reweight strategy, the cluster <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i(\theta_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i(\theta_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math> is selected based on <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. The next token <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled by randomly selecting a token within <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i(\theta_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i(\theta_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math> according to the token probability of the original language model <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{M}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{M}(\cdot|\bm{x}_{1:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. (2023)</a></cite>, we use a watermark code history <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="hist" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">hist</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure the distortion-freeness for multiple generation. If the current watermark code is in <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="hist" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">hist</annotation></semantics></math>, we will sample from the original model’s distribution instead of the watermarked distribution. The algorithm is detailed in Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Aligned Inverse Sampling. ‣ 4.2 Aligned inverse sampling ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Robust Distortion-Free Watermark for Autoregressive Audio Generation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">During detection, access to the generated audio and the watermark key <span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">key</span> is required. The token sequence <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math> is first recovered using the encoder <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> of the audio generation model. Then, for each <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,t</annotation></semantics></math>, the watermark code <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated based on the watermark key and the n-gram content. Subsequently, the pseudo-random number <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}(\theta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}(\theta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is recovered based on <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, we calculate the statistical score <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(r_{i}(\theta_{i}),x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(r_{i}(\theta_{i}),x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> following Definition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 4.2. ‣ Aligned Inverse Sampling. ‣ 4.2 Aligned inverse sampling ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Robust Distortion-Free Watermark for Autoregressive Audio Generation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. The final statistic is given by <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S(\bm{x}_{1:t})=\sum_{i=1}^{t}s(r_{i}(\theta_{i}),x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(\bm{x}_{1:t})=\sum_{i=1}^{t}s(r_{i}(\theta_{i}),x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Under the null hypothesis, <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S(\bm{x}_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(\bm{x}_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math> follows a binomial distribution with a success rate of <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have the following tail bound derived from the Hoeffding’s inequality:
<math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr(S(\bm{x}_{1:t})\geq k)\leq\exp(-2t(\frac{1}{h}-\frac{k}{t})^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(S(\bm{x}_{1:t})\geq k)\leq\exp(-2t(\frac{1}{h}-\frac{k}{t})^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. By setting a threshold on the false positive rate (e.g. FPR=1%), we can calculate a threshold <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> by solving <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(-2t(\frac{1}{h}-\frac{z}{t})^{2})=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(-2t(\frac{1}{h}-\frac{z}{t})^{2})=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. If the score <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S(\bm{x}_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(\bm{x}_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>, we reject the null hypothesis and claim that the sentence is watermarked. The detection algorithm is in Alg. <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Aligned Inverse Sampling. ‣ 4.2 Aligned inverse sampling ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Robust Distortion-Free Watermark for Autoregressive Audio Generation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Detectability comparison of watermarking methods on MMW Book Report, MMW Story, and MMW Fake News with SpiritLM. We report true positive rate at 1% and 0.1% false positive rate and the median p-value.</span></figcaption>
