<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Supplementary Experimental results.</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Detectability</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present an additional watermark detectability evaluation on the Finance QA dataset with SpiritLM in Table <a href="#A6.T24" title="Table 24 ‣ F.1 Detectability ‣ Appendix F Supplementary Experimental results. ‣ Robust Distortion-Free Watermark for Autoregressive Audio Generation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>. From Table <a href="#A6.T24" title="Table 24 ‣ F.1 Detectability ‣ Appendix F Supplementary Experimental results. ‣ Robust Distortion-Free Watermark for Autoregressive Audio Generation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> we see that <span id="A6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Aligned-IS</span> achieved the best detectability comparing with all other unbiased watermarks, at least 10% improvement on all TPR@FPR metrics. Besides, <span id="A6.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Aligned-IS</span> outperformed the biased watermarking algorithm KGW and Unigram in most cases, and achieved comparable performance with the strongly biased KGW(<math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>=2.0).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T24" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T24.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 24</span>: </span><span id="A6.T24.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Detectability for Finance QA with SpiritLM</span></figcaption>
